{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1516011-what-comments-did-time-of-judgements-receive-at-the-time-they-came-out","id":1516011,"title":"What comments did Time of Judgements receive, at the time they came out?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-24T09:00:40-07:00","id":1516011,"title":"What comments did Time of Judgements receive, at the time they came out?","content":"Nearly 20 years after ToJ came out (Jesus, time flies!), wonder what comments did they receive?<br /> <br /> Tbh from today's view, many of them are... perfunctory\u200b?<br /> <br /> Obviously, for NWoD, they want to end the whole CWoD as soon as possible (And after 8 years they picked them up again...), many hints (including that ToJ braodcast) in each line weren't used<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> News Ticker at the time (Surprisingly many guys are still active today!): <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wod-the-time-of-judgement-news-ticker.64177/\" target=\"_blank\">(WoD)The Time of Judgement News Ticker | Tabletop Roleplaying Open | RPGnet Forums</a>\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-24T09:14:29-07:00","id":1516013,"title":"","content":"One of the weirder sentiments that I can recall was one individual who was intensely livid over the fae nobles not playing a greater role in Apocalypse, in spite of those being the big names in Changeling and not really being around for Werewolf. You might still be able to see it if you dig through the rpg.net threads on the subject. It incensed me in turn, but in the opposite direction, and resulted in my being increasingly angry about Lunars being associated with Fair Folk in Exalted. Sometimes, the world is really weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-24T14:59:57-07:00","id":1516042,"title":"","content":"I remember am extensive discussion on how you actually kill an antidueluvian especially considering how apoclyptically powerful they were in Revised.<br /> <br /> Mostly i remember people being quite interested what this meant going forward. Probably worth noting nwod wasnt clear in the early stages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T03:17:09-07:00","id":1516083,"title":"","content":"Apocalypse was brilliant when it came out and I feel it has aged well. Perfunctory is a good description of Vampire, but Mage's book just felt like a missed opportunity. Mage was never about the end of the world but about what Ascension meant. It should have been a book about what is Ascension and different ways to treat it. Sure add a doomsday scenario or two if you really have to, but use that pagecount to explore the idea of Ascension itself and what it may be for the individual characters or the world itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T12:47:48-07:00","id":1516244,"title":"","content":"The Trumpet of Meru from Time of Judgment is also fun in the vein of most of the scenarios from Apocalypse - shit gets intense when the Shih get Exalted-level chi pools and don't have to worry about taking bashing for using their Bridge powers, which now have a limit of seven dots rather than five. Imbued can optionally also be a part of the fun, with all the potential infighting that implies, though they didn't get extra powers that go out to seven dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T15:04:23-07:00","id":1516262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1516011-what-comments-did-time-of-judgements-receive-at-the-time-they-came-out?p=1516244#post1516244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Trumpet of Meru from Time of Judgment is also fun in the vein of most of the scenarios from Apocalypse - shit gets intense when the Shih get Exalted-level chi pools and don't have to worry about taking bashing for using their Bridge powers, which now have a limit of seven dots rather than five. Imbued can optionally also be a part of the fun, with all the potential infighting that implies, though they didn't get extra powers that go out to seven dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Always thought that was a hillarious scenario to play through. But never saw anyone do much with that...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T15:25:03-07:00","id":1516266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1516011-what-comments-did-time-of-judgements-receive-at-the-time-they-came-out?p=1516262#post1516262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Always thought that was a hillarious scenario to play through. But never saw anyone do much with that...</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;What do you mean 'he has way more blood left'? Cauldron should totally have boiled all of his blood by now! This is a mortal that we're talking about!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T18:16:02-07:00","id":1516395,"title":"","content":"I recall the writer of one of the Mage scenarios (the one featuring Voormas) throwing a hissyfit on the old White Wolf forums and publicly bashing another scenario (the one featuring the Aswadim). It was hilarious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T03:46:25-07:00","id":1516426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1516011-what-comments-did-time-of-judgements-receive-at-the-time-they-came-out?p=1516395#post1516395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recall the writer of one of the Mage scenarios (the one featuring Voormas) throwing a hissyfit on the old White Wolf forums and publicly bashing another scenario (the one featuring the Aswadim). It was hilarious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol really? That sounds hilarious. What was his beef?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T05:37:54-07:00","id":1516440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1516011-what-comments-did-time-of-judgements-receive-at-the-time-they-came-out?p=1516426#post1516426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lol really? That sounds hilarious. What was his beef?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a vague recollection of this, but I'd love a reminder! I do feel that the OP authors interacting today are much nicer to each other and to the people, the level of conflict on usenet and the old forums could get downright nasty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T19:39:08-07:00","id":1516853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1516011-what-comments-did-time-of-judgements-receive-at-the-time-they-came-out?p=1516426#post1516426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lol really? That sounds hilarious. What was his beef?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bear in mind my memories of this are nearly two decades old, but I think it was a mix of general egotistical snobbery and nerdrage about the published stats of the Unnamed violating some of the limits of Mage mechanics. Cause the world's oldest black magician being able to exceed human limits after being elevated to join his masters is ridiculous, but an evil necromancer being able to steal a demon goddess' divinity and get an all-powerful never-before-mentioned artifact by writer's fiat so he could change how magic/the universe works is perfectly reasonable!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T01:29:37-07:00","id":1516863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1516011-what-comments-did-time-of-judgements-receive-at-the-time-they-came-out?p=1516853#post1516853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bear in mind my memories of this are nearly two decades old, but I think it was a mix of general egotistical snobbery and nerdrage about the published stats of the Unnamed violating some of the limits of Mage mechanics. Cause the world's oldest black magician being able to exceed human limits after being elevated to join his masters is ridiculous, but an evil necromancer being able to steal a demon goddess' divinity and get an all-powerful never-before-mentioned artifact by writer's fiat so he could change how magic/the universe works is perfectly reasonable!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Lol my recollection of the unamed was he was an nephandic oracle-something which didn't exist in mage. But who cares it obviously wasn't the 'canon' ending which was probably the first one. <br /> <br /> I must admit I've always found white wolf writters tendancy of cliquey public infighting quite bizzare but amusing. They havnt really stopped even today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T06:53:00-07:00","id":1516888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1516011-what-comments-did-time-of-judgements-receive-at-the-time-they-came-out?p=1516853#post1516853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bear in mind my memories of this are nearly two decades old, but I think it was a mix of general egotistical snobbery and nerdrage about the published stats of the Unnamed violating some of the limits of Mage mechanics. Cause the world's oldest black magician being able to exceed human limits after being elevated to join his masters is ridiculous, but an evil necromancer being able to steal a demon goddess' divinity and get an all-powerful never-before-mentioned artifact by writer's fiat so he could change how magic/the universe works is perfectly reasonable!</div> </div> </div> </div>Not surprising since Hell on Earth was basically a railroaded mess where the only outcome was the bad end where the Unnamed won.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T01:36:17-07:00","id":1516952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1516011-what-comments-did-time-of-judgements-receive-at-the-time-they-came-out?p=1516888#post1516888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not surprising since Hell on Earth was basically a railroaded mess where the only outcome was the bad end where the Unnamed won.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasnt the best, but pretty much all the end times scenarios were railroady. A gm of mine ran a campaign were the cabal slowly became aware of the unamed and got the news out, the idea of an apocalyptic anti christ style figure as the architect of the Nephandi naturally caused quite a stir.<br /> <br /> i did find the idea of universal ascention being pretentious escapism interesting however.<br /> <br /> <br /> I've thought about running a game were the nephandi soft win the ascention war and the world becomes a lot darker because of it. Not slipping into descention but genrally being a rotten spooky place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T23:06:32-07:00","id":1517141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1516011-what-comments-did-time-of-judgements-receive-at-the-time-they-came-out?p=1516863#post1516863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lol my recollection of the unamed was he was an nephandic oracle-something which didn't exist in mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, he existed. He was introduced in MtA's first edition <i>Book of Madness</i> under the name Al-Aswad, and his influence was implied by the continued use of the term aswadim for Nephandic bodhisattvas in the revised version.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T06:13:22-07:00","id":1517869,"title":"","content":"I remember my Mage campaign destroying the Unnamed because the Hermetics in the party came to the conclusion that without a name something simply \u201cis not.\u201d (i.e. within the Hermetic paradigm and similar to Mummy Heiku\u2026 anything without a name can\u2019t exist). They then used the fragment of the world tree and a massive ritual using every mage left to cast a mind effect to the entire cosmos basically reminding everyone that that which has no name isn\u2019t real.<br /> <br /> It was cool enough I ran with it and the climax of the campaign had Wrinkle appear and consume the unnamed thereby resetting all the carnage as if it never happened and the PCs going for pizza completely oblivious to the fact they\u2019d saved the cosmos and that the Wheel had passed its nadir and was now on the slow upwards climb. There were still many challenges to come I said, but now there was hope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}